the best way to start a trip to the ever  sandstone mountains is not a paddle  steamer the Saxons steamship company has  been taking passengers to the region  since 1837 with its vintage ships it's  the world's oldest and largest paddle  steamer fleet  after just a few kilometers you can see  the distinctive sandstone cliffs the  elbe sandstone mountains are famous as a  rock climbers paradise  in the bila valley alone you can scale  239 peaks armed only with the rope and  carabiners in keeping with the  traditional sex and climbing rules  [Music]  and because most of the crags aren't  very tall even beginners and families  have a good chance of succeeding  a must see in the elbow sandstone  mountains is the stone busti bridge  built in 1851 it's a major landmark in  the region  [Music]  slightly higher on a rock plateau that  rises 240 meters above the elbow you'll  find conics time fortress one of  Europe's largest mountain fortresses  Milton's Dana 14 here you see the  cannons we still have of course there  used to be more of them the cannons were  always lined up along the wall around  the fork when times were bad nowadays  the fortress serves as an open-air  Museum of military history and offers a  fantastic view of the elbow  [Music]
 

